&lt;h2 id=&#34;ii-background-analysis&#34;&gt;II. Background Analysis
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-industry-context&#34;&gt;1. Industry Context
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;With the &amp;ldquo;Made in China 2025&amp;rdquo; strategy, the manufacturing sector is accelerating toward digitalization and intelligent transformation. Motion control technology, serving as the &amp;ldquo;brain and nervous system&amp;rdquo; of industrial automation, is widely applied in robotics, CNC machine tools, and semiconductor equipment. However, high-end markets have long been dominated by foreign vendors. Achieving self-controllability and domestic substitution in this field is critical for securing supply chains and enhancing the competitiveness of high-end equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-company-profile&#34;&gt;2. Company Profile
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Founded in 1999 by Professors Zexiang Li, Bingqiang Gao, and Hong Wu from HKUST, Googoltech is a pioneer and platform leader in China&amp;rsquo;s motion control industry. As a national high-tech enterprise, the company focuses on R&amp;amp;D in motion control, servo drives, machine vision, and industrial networking, becoming the preferred domestic brand for core control components in high-end equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;3-project-context&#34;&gt;3. Project Context
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;To address the talent gap and the disconnect between theory and practice in high-end equipment manufacturing, Googoltech established &amp;ldquo;Googol Park.&amp;rdquo; Utilizing a Project-Based Learning (PBL) model with real-world industrial projects, it provides an &amp;ldquo;Imitation-Assimilation-Optimization-Excellence&amp;rdquo; learning path. This project, based in Googol Park, involved a one-month immersive practice in the full-cycle development of an electromechanical system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;4-technical-architecture&#34;&gt;4. Technical Architecture
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project is built on Googoltech&amp;rsquo;s proprietary technical ecosystem:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motion Controller&lt;/strong&gt;: Executes complex path planning and multi-axis coordination algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Servo Drive&lt;/strong&gt;: Receives commands and drives motors with high precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industrial Fieldbus (gLink-II)&lt;/strong&gt;: Provides high-speed stable communication with 100ns synchronization precision and data redundancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Toolchain&lt;/strong&gt;: OtoStudio IDE (ST language), Janus (visual low-code), and DriverStudio (servo tuning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;iii-task-overview&#34;&gt;III. Task Overview
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-project-introduction&#34;&gt;1. Project Introduction
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The objective was to independently complete the electromechanical integration, process design, and tuning of a PCB 3-axis drilling machine. The device uses X, Y, and Z-axis precision motion for positioning and drilling, serving as a typical industrial carrier for understanding motion control applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-core-tasks-and-requirements&#34;&gt;2. Core Tasks and Requirements
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mechanical Awareness&lt;/strong&gt;: Analyze the 3-axis modules, motors, and drilling actuators to understand motion principles and load characteristics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electrical Integration&lt;/strong&gt;: Design electrical schematics and connect controllers, drives, motors, and sensors to build the hardware system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Signal Logic Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;: Define X/Y/Z control signals (Enable, Alarm, Position) and IO signals (Limits, Origin, Drill Start).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Design&lt;/strong&gt;: Define the sequence from &amp;ldquo;Standby → Homing → Precise Positioning → Drilling → Loop/End,&amp;rdquo; incorporating safety protections (E-stop, Overtravel).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-mode Control Implementation&lt;/strong&gt;:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Low-code&lt;/strong&gt;: Rapid logic implementation using Janus visual blocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Text (ST)&lt;/strong&gt;: Detailed low-level logic development via OtoStudio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;3-expected-outcomes&#34;&gt;3. Expected Outcomes
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Prototype&lt;/strong&gt;: A fully commissioned 3-axis motion control device executing precise autonomous drilling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internship Report&lt;/strong&gt;: Summary of design, integration, and tuning, including technical solutions and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certification&lt;/strong&gt;: Completion of Googol Park assessment and acquisition of the &amp;ldquo;Electromechanical System Integrated Application Technology&amp;rdquo; certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;iv-technical-route-and-solutions&#34;&gt;IV. Technical Route and Solutions
