&lt;h3 id=&#34;task-2-electromechanical-characteristic-matching&#34;&gt;Task 2: Electromechanical Characteristic Matching
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;1-core-matching-principles&#34;&gt;1. Core Matching Principles
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Power Matching&lt;/strong&gt;: Drive system max power $\geq$ 1.5–2x peak load power to prevent motor overload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inertia Matching&lt;/strong&gt;: Load-to-rotor inertia ratio $\leq$ 3 (Precision $\leq$ 1) to prevent low-frequency oscillation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speed &amp;amp; Precision&lt;/strong&gt;: Motor rated speed $\geq$ load max speed $\times$ gear ratio; encoder resolution must be 3x better than target precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;2-calculation-logic&#34;&gt;2. Calculation Logic
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equivalent Inertia&lt;/strong&gt;: $J_{eq} = J_{load} + (J_{rotor} / n^2)$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Torque Demand&lt;/strong&gt;: $T_{peak} = J_{eq} \cdot \alpha_{max} + T_{friction}$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;task-3-servo-drive-system-tuning&#34;&gt;Task 3: Servo Drive System Tuning
